go 1.26.9

// Two lines, and which one is read depends on who is asking, so both are set
// to the same release on purpose.
//
// THE TOOLCHAIN LINE is what every build of this tree uses, local and CI alike.
// In workspace mode the go command ignores a module's toolchain line, so the
// one in engine/go.mod does not govern here and a bump starts in this file.
// setup-go reads this same line through go-version-file: its parseGoVersionFile
// prefers the toolchain directive, and main.ts parses the file before it
// exports GOTOOLCHAIN, so the directive wins. CI therefore installs the
// toolchain named here at setup time and downloads nothing per run.
//
// THE GO LINE is the language floor, and it is kept level with the toolchain
// rather than left behind, for two reasons that are both about failing loudly.
// setup-go falls back to it whenever GOTOOLCHAIN is already local at parse
// time, which a second setup-go step or a workflow level env would cause, and
// that fallback is silent: with this line at 1.26.4 it would have installed a
// release carrying GO-2026-6090 and GO-2026-5972. And with GOTOOLCHAIN=local
// and an older toolchain on the path, this line is the only thing that errors
// instead of building quietly against a superseded standard library:
// "go.work requires go >= 1.26.9 (running go 1.26.6; GOTOOLCHAIN=local)".
//
// Downloads of a toolchain are verified against the checksum database, not just
// against the file server: golang.org/toolchain@v0.0.1-go1.26.9.darwin-arm64
// carries ziphash h1:u1IV5D8HPeURJjWAqzcC8QRXDJqvXlh7FpsA4lGIg1c=, which is
// what sum.golang.org publishes for it. For a toolchain the go command makes
// that lookup whatever GONOSUMDB and GOPRIVATE say, and with GOSUMDB=off it
// refuses the download instead of skipping the check. Its source names two
// exceptions, a GOPROXY that is a single file:// URL and a GIT_HTTP_USER_AGENT
// that contains proxy.golang.org. A third, GO-2026-6602, closed in go1.26.9
// and go1.27.2: until then a matching line in a sum file the command had read
// stood in for the lookup. The switch this file starts reads no sum file.
toolchain go1.26.9

use ./engine
